## Tutorials

❮ Scanner Methods

ThenextLine()method returns a string containing all of the characters up to the next new line character in the scanner, or up to the end of the scanner if there are no more new line characters.

❮ Scanner Methods

### Code Examples

```
Example
Output the contents a file line by line:
import java.io.File;  // Import the File class
import java.io.FileNotFoundException;  // Import this class to handle errors
import java.util.Scanner; // Import the Scanner class to read text files

public class ReadFile {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    try {
      File myObj = new File("filename.txt");
      Scanner myReader = new Scanner(myObj);
      while (myReader.hasNextLine()) {
        String data = myReader.nextLine();
        System.out.println(data);
      }
      myReader.close();
    } catch (FileNotFoundException e) {
      System.out.println("An error occurred.");
      e.printStackTrace();
    }
  }
}
